        " قَالَ أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) كُفُّوا أَلْسِنَتَكُمْ وَ الْزَمُوا بُيُوتَكُمْ فَإِنَّهُ لَا يُصِيبُكُمْ أَمْرٌ تَخُصُّونَ بِهِ أَبَداً وَ لَا تَزَالُ الزَّيْدِيَّةُ لَكُمْ وِقَاءً أَبَداً ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from usman Bin Isa, from the one who informed him who said, ",
          "‘Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Restrain your tongues and bind (yourselves) to your houses, so no matter would hit you specialising you with it, ever, nor would the Zaidites cease to be shielding you, ever!’"
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "13. A number of our people have narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from ‘Uthman ibn ‘Isa from those he has narrated from and who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah (a.s.) has said, ‘Control your tongues and stay home, no one will ever disturb you in particular. Zaydi people are still a protection for you and they will always be as such.’” "
        ]
      }
